New Haven is a settlement on the coast of a blood lake in the [[Geography/Althane/Lunae Badlands/Hidden Gulch/index|Gulch]], founded by [[People/Althane/Marzo|Marzo]]. He has built a city here in every cycle; it has moved, and its people have moved with it, but it has always been his. It was long called Fat Cock City and goes by New Haven now.

The present city is a mercantile town in the old style of the Gulch, with a cooper's shop and people fishing off the shore. It has become known for its plays and its storytelling, and Marzo tells the tales of the Weft there.

The blood lake is a nexus of [[Geography/Althane/Realms/Nexus|the Nexus]], and the second moon hangs directly overhead. The water smells of metal and things live in it, though the locals fish it anyway. Out in the lake stands a ziggurat, and the corpse of the [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessian]] Beast lies on its top, its power drawn off to feed [[Geography/Althane/The Thirteenth Realm|the Thirteenth Realm]]. A bridge runs from the shore to a platform at the ziggurat's foot.
